1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This video introduces the mode and editor-related updates for you.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
In the previous CLO version,

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
when adding a project file, you cannot choose the color scheme you want from the open file.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
To change the color scheme, you can only do it in the color editor after opening the file.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
From the current version, when adding a project file,

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
you can choose the color scheme you want to open.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
When you want to design a clothing style,

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
but you also want to add a specific color scheme to the current project,

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
this function is very useful.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Find the file,

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
add the project,

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
open the project file you want,

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and in the window that pops out, the color option is added below the clothing.

14
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
In the drop-down menu, select the color scheme to be added.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
You can choose all or customize it.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Click the color button on the right to select the color scheme.

17
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
It is convenient for you to see the color scheme of each color.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The color scheme of each color will be displayed as the most fabric used in the clothing.

19
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Please note that the file created in the 2025.0 or earlier version

20
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
will only display the name of the color scheme and not the color scheme.

21
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,000
If you choose all,

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
the color scheme of the file you have added and the file you have added

23
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
will be saved in the order of the project file.

24
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Click the same order to combine.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Therefore, if you want them to match each other,

26
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
in both project files,

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
the color scheme is very important in the same order and preservation.

28
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Please note that if you want to add less color schemes

29
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
to the projects that already have more color schemes,

30
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
you will use the first color scheme to fill in the remaining color schemes.

31
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
As usual,

32
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
when you want to customize the color scheme,

33
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
find the file, increase the project,

34
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
open the project file you want,

35
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
click the right button at the bottom of the clothing in the pop-up window,

36
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
open the color list to select the color scheme you want to add,

37
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
then the file will be combined according to the color scheme selected.

38
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
For example, I have now selected the second and third colors of the swimsuit suit.

39
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
After adding,

40
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
they will be added to the first two color schemes of the current project.

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The first color scheme selected by the added project

42
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
is the color scheme 2 and black in this case,

43
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
which will always be the combat suit,

44
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
and will combine with the remaining color schemes in the current project.

45
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
In the future, more options will be added

46
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
to be able to mix and match the color scheme of different projects.

47
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
This update can help users improve the work efficiency of color combination design.

48
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,000
In the latest version of CLO,

49
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
we optimized the key frame animation settings.

50
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
The main improvements include

51
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
the color key frame animation that supports the twist material,

52
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
the key frame animation that lights up in the Vray rendering,

53
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
and the new time-limited selection layer function.

54
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Open the color editor,

55
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
add the key frame to each color animation column,

56
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
and add the key frame animation to each color animation column.

57
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Then click the play preview effect.

58
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You can see that the color key frame is applied,

59
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
the color of the twist and the color of the twist is changed.

60
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
This makes the animation transition more natural.

61
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Open the rendering window,

62
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
render lighting settings.

63
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
You can see that the light bulb icon has now been removed,

64
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
but you can use the fire option to replace it.

65
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
After using the fire option, you can also set more content.

66
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Users can add key frames to each of the following settings,

67
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
such as intensity, angle, color, width and height, etc.

68
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Here, the light bulb key frame is added to the animation.

69
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Then set the key frame to the following options.

70
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
You can control the strength and angle of different stages of lighting in the animation.

71
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:26,000
This can be used to adjust the light bulb.

72
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
In addition, we have also improved the control of the circle size setting.

73
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
After starting this setting,

74
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
you can also edit the radius,

75
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
head shadow height and ground mix settings.

76
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
And each setting can be added to the key frame.

77
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Finally, you can adjust the time range of the current animation.

78
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Click on the right on the animation layer.

79
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Select to limit the time range to the selected layer.

80
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
You can see that the play area will be adjusted to the selected layer range.

81
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Finally, select to finally render the animation.

82
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You can get the animation of the twist color and light.

83
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:20,000
I hope these updates can improve your animation experience and simplify your workflow.

84
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:31,000
In the previous version, the project with GLTF format is not supported by the virtual model animation.

85
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Therefore, any joint animation applied to virtual models or animation based on storage will not be saved.

86
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Thank you for watching.

87
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:44,000
In the new version, you can now choose to include virtual model animation.

88
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
This optimization provides greater flexibility for animation processing.

89
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:56,000
So you can easily integrate virtual models into various platforms or workflow.

90
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Find the file and select to export GLTF 2.0 GLTF.

91
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:09,000
In the window, select all virtual models.

92
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
In the options below, select virtual model animation.

93
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Select the animation type you want.

94
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:23,000
When you want to keep the structure of Google to edit or play in the future, this is an ideal choice.

95
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:28,000
To bind Google's model, the best choice is to implement the high guarantee animation.

96
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:33,000
You can flexibly choose the export settings that are most suitable for your project needs.

97
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
To get better compatibility files.

98
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Whether you are dedicated to interactive experience or high-quality visual display.

99
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:51,000
This function can make you more free to create and perform virtual model animation.

100
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Thank you for watching.

